<title>NETHERLANDS: TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY MEN/WOMEN SECOND DAY RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-HEINEKEN TROPHY MEN/WOMEN SECOND DAY RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ROSMALEN, Netherlands 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the third day of the Heineken Trophy combined $500,000 ATP men's and $175,000 WTA women's grass court tennis tournament on Wednesday (prefix number denotes seed):</p>
<p>Men's second round:</p>
<p>1-Michael Chang (U.S) beat Alex Radulescu (Germany) 7-6 (7-5) 6-1</p>
<p>8-Francisco Clavet (Spain) beat Hicham Arazi (Morocco) 6-3 0-6 6-1</p>
<p>4-Jonas Bjorkman (Sweden) beat Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Fernon Wibier (Netherlands) beat 6-Magnus Gustafsson (Sweden) 7-6 (7-5) 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>Women's second round:</p>
<p>1-Anke Huber (Germany) beat Sandra Kleinova (Czech Republic) 6-4 2-6 6-4</p>
<p>6-Dominique van Roost (Belgium) beat Kristie Boogert (Netherlands) 2-6 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>3-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat Barbara Rittner (Germany) 6-1 2-0 (Rittner retired injured)</p>
<p>2-Mary Pierce (France) beat Sarah Pitkowski (France) 6-3 7-5</p>
<p>5-Sabine Appelmans (Belgium) beat Florencia Labat (Argentina) 7-5 7-5</p>
<p>Miriam Oremans (Netherlands) beat Magdalena Maleeva (Bulgaria) 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>4-Karina Habsudova (Slovakia) beat Patricia Hy-Boulais (Canada) 2-6 7-5 6-4</p>
</text>
